      "crFrom": null,
      "crTo": null,
      "workDone": "(S/L Section) Dn Home Signal S30 and Calling-on Signal S30A were not obeyed for Dn 77212 Passenger. As per data logger report, S30 RLR and S30A RLR relays were not picked up.\nUpon checking by JE/S/JMDG and staff, it was observed that S30 RLR and S30A RLR relays were not pickedup as in their circuit, the drop contacts of S3–30A UYR1, UYR2, UYR3, and UYR4 relays were required. However, these relays remained in the picked-up state even after completion of the previous Up train movement.\nFurther detailed checking revealed that in relay room, S3/4/5/8 ASPR4 relay was in the dropped condition as in its circuit, the S3/4/5/8 ASR relay C7–C8 front contact was offering high resistance (1.08 MΩ). Due to this, even though S3/4/5/8 ASR relay was picked up, S3–30A UYR1, UYR2, UYR3, and UYR4 relays did not drop, as a stick path was continuously offered through the drop contact of S3/4/5/8 ASPR4 relay.\nThe defective relay was replaced and Signals were tested and normal working was restored.\n",
